1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:22,542
The first time I drove my police Lamborghini into the clouds, the sky
opened up and a woman told me I was already late for my own award. I
had not enrolled yet. Nigga, I hadn't found the parking lot. Some
other nigga was already polishing a prize for me while I was trying to
work out whether this cloud counted as a turn.

2
00:00:22,792 --> 00:00:42,959
Tank called from the Mercedes behind us. This nigga said you late for
an award? Woman said it. Aiden, nigga, don't get technical in heaven.
What you win? I don't know yet. How this nigga win something he don't
know? Shawna leaned toward the phone. Tank, you've met him. That
settled the question.

3
00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:59,752
I heard my nigga laugh, heard Rosa laugh beside him, heard the
Mercedes engine rise through the white air. A nigga could get used to
that sound: all his people following because the impossible road had
finally decided to hold his weight.

4
00:01:00,002 --> 00:01:14,542
Shawna sat beside me with her bare feet on the dashboard and a pair of
white sunglasses bigger than the sins we had committed on our
honeymoon. She had a new diamond on her wedding finger and Dante's old
watch on her wrist.

5
00:01:14,792 --> 00:01:40,808
I had my badge in my pocket, his cross under my shirt, and a twelve-
cylinder reason to believe the universe had finally gotten serious
about respecting me. The invitation said Sky High Advanced Hero
Academy. A postgraduate program for heroes who had already graduated
and somehow still wanted homework. It said my rescue in Vegas had
demonstrated exceptional aptitude.

6
00:01:41,058 --> 00:02:06,745
Exceptional aptitude was when you parallel parked without touching the
curb. I had driven through a burning auditorium and still delivered my
valedictorian speech before the principal finished crying. They should
have put exceptional motherfucker. Aiden, Shawna said. Cloud. Baby, I
see it. Inside the car. A little piece of weather rolled through the
open window and rested on her lap.

7
00:02:06,995 --> 00:02:27,237
She pushed her sunglasses down and stared at it. The cloud drifted
over her wedding ring, turned pink, and dissolved. Your diamonds doing
shit to the climate now, I said. Keep looking at the road. There was
no road. That was the first issue. There had been a road until thirty
seconds ago.

8
00:02:27,487 --> 00:02:49,525
It had climbed a mountain, passed between two stone lions, and ended
at a gate reading WELCOME, HEROES. Then a guard in silver armor had
glanced at my gold badge, looked at my face, and saluted so hard his
helmet fell off. Captain Aiden, he'd said. It's an honor. Nigga, which
way? Up. I had appreciated his confidence.

9
00:02:49,775 --> 00:03:12,993
Now the Lamborghini was climbing an invisible ramp through the clouds
at a speed Shawna described as why the fuck. The wheel vibrated in my
hands. Beneath us, the mountains shrank until they looked like
somebody's pile of dirty clothes. Behind us Tank's black Mercedes rose
through the mist. Rosa sat beside him, singing into a hairbrush.

10
00:03:13,243 --> 00:03:30,859
Marcellus was in the back wearing a gray suit, carrying a small case,
and looking as if he had already decided heaven charged too much for
lunch. Dr. Vega had come for a three-day visit and was currently
holding Tank's headrest like she intended to remove it.

11
00:03:31,109 --> 00:03:53,252
Mercedes and Porsche followed in a red convertible I had bought them
after they pointed out that I owned an island's worth of cars and kept
asking them to share an Uber. The women were arguing over whose turn
it was to meet a man who could fly. All my people were ascending. And
at the top of the clouds waited a whole fucking city.

12
00:03:53,502 --> 00:04:17,841
Not a building. A city. White towers rose around a stadium shaped like
a golden shield. A glass train moved between them without touching
anything. Gardens hung off stone balconies. An enormous waterfall
poured from one edge of the island and disappeared into blue air.
Little vehicles streamed across bridges suspended between floating
blocks of land.

13
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:43,540
Farther out, a ring of separate islands carried hotels, stores, and a
casino with a flashing sign visible from what appeared to be several
religions. SKY HIGH stood over the front gate in letters taller than
my mansion. I slowed down just enough for the Lamborghini to make its
noise. Shawna smiled. There he go. Who? My husband about to introduce
himself to the atmosphere.

14
00:04:43,790 --> 00:05:08,951
Baby, the atmosphere been waiting. The invisible ramp became a solid
white drive. Students stopped where they were. A man with transparent
wings folded them and turned. A woman carrying three refrigerators
over her head looked at me and forgot she was carrying refrigerators.
Somebody in a crimson cape walked straight into a fountain. I parked
in front of the main staircase.

15
00:05:09,201 --> 00:05:32,496
There was a gold sign. DEAN. I read it carefully and remained parked.
Tank pulled up beside my door, lowered his window, and looked at the
sign. Then at the car. Then back at the sign, giving the English
language every opportunity to save me. Nigga, you know somebody named
Dean? Could be welcoming me by position. Your position is illegally
parked.

16
00:05:32,746 --> 00:05:57,354
Shawna reached across me and tapped the horn. Once. A tiny, expensive
note of warning. Move the car, Aiden. Baby, let me establish a
relationship. Nigga, with reverse. Behind Tank, Porsche had stopped
sideways to take a picture. Mercedes leaned across her and
straightened the phone. Get the sign in it. This nigga gonna claim
they reserved it. They might.

17
00:05:57,604 --> 00:06:19,098
Then we got a before picture, Mercedes said. Rosa came over, read
DEAN, and hooked her arm through Shawna's. Girl, first day and your
husband already trying to graduate the administration. I dressed him
myself. I thought that would use up the difficult part. Nigga came
accessorized with a jurisdiction, Tank said.

18
00:06:19,348 --> 00:06:44,412
I opened my door with the dignity available to a man being publicly
coordinated by everybody he loved. My shoe touched white stone. The
engine settled into a low, satisfied rumble. Listen to that, I said.
Car agrees. That nigga burns gasoline, Shawna said. He'll agree with a
garage fire. Tank bent down toward the exhaust. You happy, little
nigga?

19
00:06:44,662 --> 00:07:08,827
Don't talk to my car like that. I'm establishing a relationship. The
women broke. Rosa leaned into Shawna. Mercedes lowered the phone
because she couldn't keep it steady. Even Vega loosened one hand from
Tank's headrest. There it was: one decent laugh, and suddenly we had
ground under us again, even up here. I could work with that. Then
somebody above us cleared her throat.

20
00:07:09,077 --> 00:07:30,464
Every nigga in our arrival committee remembered we were parked in
front of a school. A tall woman descended the steps wearing a white
suit with silver lightning along the collar. Her hair fell black to
her shoulders except for one white streak. She had the kind of face
that made a man stand up straighter before he remembered he had a wife
beside him.

21
00:07:30,714 --> 00:07:54,770
The air sharpened around her. Her eyes were gray, and behind the gray
something bright moved. Captain Aiden, she said. I stepped out. Dean.
Seraphine Storm. That's a hell of a name. I earned it. So did I. We
shook hands. A tiny spark jumped between us. I did not let go. Her
eyebrow rose. Most visitors flinch. Most visitors ain't me.

22
00:07:55,020 --> 00:08:19,610
Shawna came around the car. Storm's attention moved to her ring, then
to her face. Mrs. Aiden. Shawna. They shook hands without sparks. I
respected the weather for knowing when to behave. Tank parked behind
me. Nigga, you in her space. I know where I'm at. We can arrange
another space, Storm said. Tank looked from her to me and slowly took
off his sunglasses.

23
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:43,836
We just got here. I make a strong first impression. From the staircase
a blond man in a blue uniform laughed once. He was broad through the
shoulders, clean-shaven, with a silver emblem on his chest and a jaw
he plainly expected other people to remember. That's the famous
graduate? he asked. Storm didn't look away from me. Victor Voltage.
Twenty-seven.

24
00:08:44,086 --> 00:09:08,688
First in his division until this morning. Victor's smile stopped. My
smile began. Nigga, don't look at me. I ain't touched your division.
Your provisional placement puts you first overall, Storm told me.
Based on what? Victor demanded. She gestured toward the Lamborghini.
He looked at the car as if it had personally stolen his childhood.
That's a vehicle.

25
00:09:08,938 --> 00:09:34,707
The entrance ramp was closed, Storm said. Everybody got quiet. I
looked back at the sky. Tank looked back at the sky. Shawna took off
her sunglasses very slowly. Aiden. Now hold on. Storm's smile grew. We
were testing our emergency magnetic ascent field. You drove through
its narrowest boundary at exactly the velocity required to remain
inside it.

26
00:09:34,957 --> 00:09:57,563
Then three civilian cars followed your path. Dr. Vega got out of the
Mercedes. I would like to go home. You can use the open ramp, Storm
said. There was an open ramp? I put my arm around Shawna. Baby, I
brought us the scenic way. She pinched my side. The old wound still
had opinions about people touching it.

27
00:09:57,813 --> 00:10:24,020
The scenic way to fucking death. And look how beautiful we survived.
Then the sky train exploded. Not the whole train. The front coupling
burst in orange flame as it came around the stadium. A sharp crack
punched across the courtyard. Heads turned. A hundred windows flashed.
The train tilted. Forty people screamed at once. Victor was moving
before the sound finished.

28
00:10:24,270 --> 00:10:46,866
Blue-white energy wrapped his fists. He launched himself upward, fast
enough to knock spray out of the fountain. Storm raised both hands.
Wind slammed through the courtyard. The train's front carriage lurched
back toward its rail. The rear two kept falling. I saw a woman pressed
to the back window. Saw a man drag another man off the floor.

29
00:10:47,116 --> 00:11:08,156
Saw the distance between that train and the edge of the island
closing. Nigga, I was supposed to be receiving something. Instead I
had to go earn it again. I jumped into the Lamborghini. Tank! He
already had the Mercedes door open. Shawna slid into my passenger
seat. You staying here, I said. Drive.

30
00:11:08,406 --> 00:11:30,700
Baby— Those people do not have time for you to win this argument. I
hit the gas. The car shot between the fountain and the steps. Somebody
tried to tell me that was a pedestrian path. He said the first half to
the windshield and the second half to the exhaust. The rear carriages
struck a maintenance platform beyond the stadium. Metal shrieked.

31
00:11:30,950 --> 00:11:56,710
The platform bent toward the open air. Victor hovered above it, both
arms spread, electricity coursing into the damaged suspension rings.
Sweat ran down his face. His boots flickered. He was powerful. He was
also holding forty people over a drop nobody had bothered measuring
for survivability. I understood his problem immediately. Too many
niggas. Not enough ground.

32
00:11:56,960 --> 00:12:22,004
I took a turn so hard Shawna's hair whipped across my mouth. The
Lamborghini climbed a service stair, hit the landing, and flew over a
strip of garden. We landed on the maintenance platform with a crash
that made my teeth feel individually expensive. The platform dipped.
Get that car off! Victor shouted. I looked through the windshield at
the hanging carriage. Shawna. Door.

33
00:12:22,254 --> 00:12:47,740
She unbuckled. Which? All of them. I shoved the Lamborghini nose
beneath a sloping support beam. The hood buckled. A warning screamed
from the dashboard. I kept going until the car wedged between the
broken platform and the stone service wall. The platform stopped
dropping. Victor stared at me. Nigga, I shouted, keep doing the light
shit! Shawna was already at the carriage.

34
00:12:47,990 --> 00:13:11,017
She hit its emergency release, hauled the door open, and caught the
first woman through it by both arms. Walk toward the wall, she
ordered. Keep your hands on the rail. Don't look down. Somebody looked
down and froze. My wife slapped him. Look at me instead. He did. He
moved. Tank brought the Mercedes onto solid ground and jumped out.
Rosa followed him.

35
00:13:11,267 --> 00:13:34,606
She took one look at the gap and began singing, loud and steady, a
beat people could move to. Not a sad song. One of the nasty ones she
performed in Vegas when men forgot how much cash they had brought.
Forty terrified adult heroes began crossing a ruined platform to a
song about getting paid before breakfast. I climbed onto my hood.

36
00:13:34,856 --> 00:13:59,113
It was an expensive hood. I would mourn it when niggas stopped falling
out of the sky. Inside the last carriage, a man had his leg trapped
beneath a fallen seat. A silver-haired woman knelt beside him. One
whole side of the carriage was opening over empty blue air. I jumped
through the door. The woman looked at my badge. Are you rescue? Today.

37
00:13:59,363 --> 00:14:23,607
I grabbed the seat. It didn't move. The trapped man said, My power's
density. I can't turn it off when I'm scared. How heavy? A lot. Nigga,
that is a terrible number. The train shifted. Outside, Victor yelled.
A burst of blue light turned the windows white. I braced my shoes
against the opposite seat and pulled. The metal bit my palms. Nothing.

38
00:14:23,857 --> 00:14:48,427
The man shook so hard the floor rattled. I got close to his face.
What's your name? Elias. Elias, listen to me. My wife standing outside
this train. He blinked. That woman thinks I'm the greatest man alive.
I happen to agree. Now you gonna make both of us look stupid? No. Then
stop trying to weigh more than my reputation. He laughed. Just once.

39
00:14:48,677 --> 00:15:11,625
A frightened little cough of a laugh. The floor lifted. I tore the
seat aside. There we fucking go. The woman helped me drag him. We
reached the door as the back window broke away. Wind hit us. My cross
slapped against my chest. Below, the waterfall hung like a white
ribbon all the way into the clouds. Victor's left hand went dark.

40
00:15:11,875 --> 00:15:37,327
The carriage dropped six inches. I shoved Elias through the door into
Tank's arms. The woman followed. I grabbed the rail. Then the platform
tore loose. My Lamborghini went with it. For one ugly second I saw my
whole future reflected in that dark blue roof: car gone, wife
watching, nigga floating down to Earth with a gold badge and an unpaid
insurance argument.

41
00:15:37,577 --> 00:16:03,503
Shawna caught my wrist. Tank caught her waist. Storm's wind caught the
car. Everything stopped. Not gently. My shoulder made a noise. Shawna
swore. Tank planted his feet and shouted, I got all you motherfuckers!
The dean stood at the end of the broken walkway with lightning in her
hair. The entire Lamborghini hung sideways beneath us inside a
spinning cradle of cloud.

42
00:16:03,753 --> 00:16:27,559
Captain, she said through clenched teeth. Would you please stop adding
weight? I hauled myself up beside my wife. I'm trying to take some
off. Victor brought the last carriage down into the grass. Storm
lowered my car beside it. The engine ticked. The left headlight hung
out like a tired eye. Silence spread over the service yard. Then Elias
began clapping.

43
00:16:27,809 --> 00:16:52,079
The silver-haired woman joined him. By the time I stood up, everybody
was doing it. Shawna grabbed my face and kissed me hard enough to
settle the disagreement we had not finished in the car. I held her
against me. Around us forty rescued people cheered louder. That's my
husband, she said when she pulled back. Nobody argued. Victor landed
beside the wrecked train.

44
00:16:52,329 --> 00:17:16,317
His uniform smoked at the wrists. He looked at the Lamborghini. Looked
at my bleeding hands. Looked at Shawna holding me. You have no powers,
he said. I got several good qualities. No. I mean you have no
measurable power signature. Nigga, measure the people who ain't dead.
His mouth opened. Then he looked at Elias sitting safely on the grass.
He closed it.

45
00:17:16,567 --> 00:17:42,859
Storm came toward me. Her hair settled. Behind her, students poured
around the corner, calling to the passengers, filming the wreckage,
shouting my name even though I had introduced myself to approximately
four people. Your award ceremony, the dean said, will now include an
additional citation. I looked at my car. Will it include a body shop?
The best engineering faculty in the sky. Good.

46
00:17:43,109 --> 00:18:06,882
That nigga need a doctor. Dr. Vega stepped around Tank carrying a
medical bag. The car can wait. You are bleeding. Little bit. That is
also a terrible number. She took my hand. Shawna stood against my
other side. Tank looked at the shattered platform and shook his head
with a smile he couldn't hide. You been here twelve minutes. Thirteen,
Storm said. See?

47
00:18:07,132 --> 00:18:30,541
I told him. I gave the school an extra minute. At the edge of the
crowd stood a thin man in a charcoal suit. He had silver hair combed
straight back, a black cane, and eyes that did not seem interested in
blinking. Two guards stood behind him in uniforms darker than the
others. Storm noticed him and straightened. Chancellor Voss.

48
00:18:30,791 --> 00:18:54,621
He approached the broken coupling first. Bent his head. Touched a
scorched piece of metal with one gloved finger. Then he turned to me.
An extraordinary arrival. We try. His smile showed no teeth. You saved
a number of people whose gifts are important to this institution. I
glanced at Elias. He was holding the silver-haired woman's hand.

49
00:18:54,871 --> 00:19:16,640
His whole body shook now that it was allowed to. Saved the rest too.
Naturally. Voss's eyes moved to my badge, then my cross, then Shawna.
He lingered on none of them long enough for me to call it a problem.
But a nigga can feel a problem dressing itself. We will investigate
the equipment failure, he said. Do that.

50
00:19:16,890 --> 00:19:40,810
His guards collected the broken coupling before anybody else touched
it. Storm watched them go. Her face had changed for one second, then
changed back. She offered us the grand staircase, the open doors, the
city of people waiting to meet me. I put my good arm around Shawna.
Tank lifted my overnight bag from the ruined car. Rosa took his other
arm.

51
00:19:41,060 --> 00:20:04,181
Marcellus appeared carrying the case he had somehow never set down.
First impression? he asked. Strong, I said. He looked at the wrecked
train, then at the whole school applauding. I should have brought a
larger safe. We went up those steps together. Above the entrance hung
a banner they had apparently prepared before I arrived. WELCOME,
EXCEPTIONAL HEROES.

52
00:20:04,431 --> 00:20:27,458
Somebody was already climbing a ladder to change it. I didn't tell
them to. Nigga, excellence makes suggestions of its own. Our rooms
occupied the top floor of a tower overlooking the western edge. There
were two balconies, a bath large enough to qualify for boat ownership,
and a bedroom ceiling that showed the actual stars above the clouds.

53
00:20:27,708 --> 00:20:48,336
The bellman set down our bags and waited to be tipped. I gave him
enough money to change the direction of his afternoon. He looked at
it. Looked at me. Sir, I have worked here eleven years. Then you was
overdue. He left walking backward. Shawna closed the door and leaned
against it. Her smile had gone soft.

54
00:20:48,586 --> 00:21:08,482
That was the one that always made me feel more dangerous and less
prepared at the same time. You scared me, she said. I had it. I know
you had it. That's not the same thing. I crossed the room. She put her
hands beneath my open jacket and rested them against my ribs, careful
of the old hurt.

55
00:21:08,732 --> 00:21:29,666
Outside the balcony a woman flew past carrying a bouquet larger than
herself. Somewhere below us people were still shouting about the
train. You came with me, I said. Always. Even when I'm parking wrong.
Especially. Apparently that's when you become first in your class. I
kissed her forehead. Then her mouth.

56
00:21:29,916 --> 00:21:52,661
She pulled me closer, and for a little while the biggest thing
happening in the sky was our door staying shut. Later, when we stood
on the balcony wearing the school's expensive robes, I saw a second
city beneath the first. It wasn't really a city. More a collection of
black buildings suspended under the island's lower rock. Bridges
joined them.

57
00:21:52,911 --> 00:22:16,390
Red lights burned along their roofs. One tower descended farther than
the rest and ended in a circular chamber that glowed through its
windows like a covered furnace. What's that? Shawna asked. Basement
with ambition. A train moved along a track beneath it. The cars had no
windows. She stopped smiling. The train entered the glowing chamber.

58
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:39,622
For a moment the windows turned a strange yellow-white. Then every
light went out together. Above us, music began on the school lawn.
People laughed. Somebody sent a ribbon of purple fire curling between
two towers. Shawna rested her head against my shoulder. Tomorrow, she
said, I'm finding somebody who'll tell me what that is.

59
00:22:39,872 --> 00:22:47,464
I looked at the dark place under all our beautiful rooms. Tomorrow, I
said, I'm getting my fucking car back.
